Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:34:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] amd/addrlib: no AVX2 swizzlers in the PS4 console build

The PS4's CPU (Jaguar) has AVX but no AVX2, and clang declares only the
intrinsics of the features a Sony target compiles for, so
addrswizzler.cpp's [[gnu::target("avx2")]] functions do not compile
there. The console build leaves AddrLib's SIMD paths out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R3DbSodVLhQVcvZSazbPue
---
 src/amd/addrlib/meson.build | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/addrlib/meson.build b/src/amd/addrlib/meson.build
index 4f673b4..f113e00 100644
--- a/src/amd/addrlib/meson.build
+++ b/src/amd/addrlib/meson.build
@@ -49,7 +49,10 @@ files_addrlib = files(
 )
 
 # Skip the addrlib definition of ADDR_FASTCALL so as not to use regparm.
-cpp_args_addrlib = ['-DADDR_FASTCALL=', '-DADDR_ALLOW_SIMD=1']
+# The PS4's CPU (Jaguar) has no AVX2, and its compiler declares only the
+# intrinsics of the features it targets, so the AVX2 swizzlers are left out.
+cpp_args_addrlib = ['-DADDR_FASTCALL=',
+                    '-DADDR_ALLOW_SIMD=@0@'.format(with_radv_ps4_console ? 0 : 1)]
 
 if host_machine.endian() == 'little'
   cpp_args_addrlib += '-DLITTLEENDIAN_CPU'
